WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.667 --> 00:00:03.434
-Welcome, welcome, welcome to
"The Tonight Show," everybody.

00:00:03.434 --> 00:00:08.033
Here we are.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:08.033 --> 00:00:10.100
Let's get to some news.

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:12.234
Well, guys, last night
President Biden delivered

00:00:12.234 --> 00:00:15.167
his first State of the Union
address.

00:00:15.167 --> 00:00:17.567
Biden spoke for 62 minutes.

00:00:17.567 --> 00:00:20.901
Well, actually he spoke for
10 with 52 minutes of clapping.

00:00:20.901 --> 00:00:22.167
[ Laughter ]

00:00:22.167 --> 00:00:24.601
-So every child, every American
has clean water

00:00:24.601 --> 00:00:26.667
to drink at home and at school.

00:00:26.667 --> 00:00:28.968
[ Applause ]

00:00:28.968 --> 00:00:32.601
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:32.601 --> 00:00:35.601
Biden's speech aired on
every major TV network.

00:00:35.601 --> 00:00:37.100
When they heard,
Netflix was like,

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:39.167
"See, this is why we can charge
whatever we want."

00:00:39.167 --> 00:00:40.567
[ Laughter ]

00:00:40.567 --> 00:00:42.467
Of course,
Biden kicked off his speech

00:00:42.467 --> 00:00:44.601
talking about the war
in Ukraine.

00:00:44.601 --> 00:00:46.601
And in a rare moment
of bipartisanship,

00:00:46.601 --> 00:00:48.767
both parties
stood and applauded.

00:00:48.767 --> 00:00:50.767
Yep. Democrats clapped proudly

00:00:50.767 --> 00:00:52.868
while Republicans were like,
"Please don't show me on camera.

00:00:52.868 --> 00:00:55.467
Please don't show me on camera."
[ Laughter ]

00:00:55.467 --> 00:00:57.701
Yeah, everyone seemed to be
in support of Biden.

00:00:57.701 --> 00:00:59.501
Well, almost everyone.

00:00:59.501 --> 00:01:01.000
Throughout his speech,
representatives

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:03.367
Marjorie Taylor Greene
and Lauren Boebert

00:01:03.367 --> 00:01:05.000
were heckling Biden.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:06.801
Here they are right here.

00:01:06.801 --> 00:01:10.133
Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:10.133 --> 00:01:12.901
They're like the QAnon
Statler and Waldorf.

00:01:12.901 --> 00:01:15.133
[ Laughter ]

00:01:15.133 --> 00:01:17.868
Look, I feel bad for
the congressman

00:01:17.868 --> 00:01:19.467
stuck in between them.
Look at that guy.

00:01:19.467 --> 00:01:23.300
[ Laughter ]

00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:26.367
Seriously, you think the middle
seat on Spirit Airlines is bad.

00:01:26.367 --> 00:01:29.534
[ Laughter ]

00:01:29.534 --> 00:01:30.901
And everyone's
talking about this.

00:01:30.901 --> 00:01:32.601
At the very end of his speech,

00:01:32.601 --> 00:01:34.801
Biden said something that
stood out to people.

00:01:34.801 --> 00:01:36.133
Check this out.

00:01:36.133 --> 00:01:40.300
-God bless you all and may God
protect our troops.

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:42.434
Thank you.

00:01:42.434 --> 00:01:44.167
Go get him!

00:01:44.167 --> 00:01:48.167
[ Laughter ]

00:01:48.167 --> 00:01:50.868
-"Go get him"?

00:01:50.868 --> 00:01:52.667
"Go get him"?
-"Go get him."

00:01:52.667 --> 00:01:53.734
[ Laughter ]

00:01:53.734 --> 00:01:56.067
-Not "go get 'em."

00:01:56.067 --> 00:01:57.834
"Go get him." Yeah.

00:01:57.834 --> 00:01:59.000
[ Laughter ]

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:00.601
Right after, Putin called Trump

00:02:00.601 --> 00:02:02.167
and was like,
"Is he talking about me?

00:02:02.167 --> 00:02:03.634
Is he talking about me?
What is "--

00:02:03.634 --> 00:02:06.434
[ Laughter ]

00:02:06.434 --> 00:02:08.601
Well, Senator Chuck Schumer
was there,

00:02:08.601 --> 00:02:11.534
and he took home the award
for most poorly timed applause.

00:02:11.534 --> 00:02:12.601
Watch this.

00:02:12.601 --> 00:02:14.400
-Unlike the $2 trillion tax cut

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:17.234
passed in the previous
administration that benefited

00:02:17.234 --> 00:02:22.367
the top 1% of Americans,
the American Rescue Plan --

00:02:22.367 --> 00:02:24.567
The American Rescue Plan

00:02:24.567 --> 00:02:27.534
helped working people
and left no one behind.

00:02:27.534 --> 00:02:29.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:29.067 --> 00:02:32.501
-Yeah, the medical term for that
is "premature ovation."

00:02:32.501 --> 00:02:34.367
-Whoa! Hey!
[ Laughter ]

00:02:34.367 --> 00:02:36.801
-And Speaker Nancy Pelosi
didn't go home empty-handed.

00:02:36.801 --> 00:02:39.067
She won the award
for weirdest clap.

00:02:39.067 --> 00:02:42.100
Here it is.

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:44.033
-Many of you have been there.

00:02:44.033 --> 00:02:48.400
I've been in and out of Iraq
and Afghanistan over 40 times.

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:52.467
[ Laughter ]

00:02:52.467 --> 00:02:54.968
-Is there a knuckle rub
TikTok challenge

00:02:54.968 --> 00:02:57.267
that we don't know about?

00:02:57.267 --> 00:02:59.400
It looked like she was shaking
invisible maracas.

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:02.567
I don't know what she was doing.

00:03:02.567 --> 00:03:05.667
And this was great -- Supreme
Court Justice Stephen Breyer

00:03:05.667 --> 00:03:08.634
definitely won the award for
"guy who looks like the waiters

00:03:08.634 --> 00:03:11.434
at Applebee's are singing him
happy birthday." Look at this.

00:03:11.434 --> 00:03:13.234
-Thank you for your service.

00:03:13.234 --> 00:03:15.133
Thank you, thank you, thank you.

00:03:15.133 --> 00:03:16.434
[ Applause ]

00:03:16.434 --> 00:03:18.033
I mean it.

00:03:18.033 --> 00:03:20.601
Get up. Stand up. Let's see you.

00:03:20.601 --> 00:03:21.968
Thank you.

00:03:21.968 --> 00:03:26.801
[ Applause continues ]

00:03:26.801 --> 00:03:29.567
[ Laughter ]

00:03:29.567 --> 00:03:32.067
[ Rim shot ]

00:03:32.067 --> 00:03:39.734
[ Laughter ]

00:03:39.734 --> 00:03:42.701
-Switching gears here,
Major League Baseball

00:03:42.701 --> 00:03:46.133
has canceled opening day
and some regular season games

00:03:46.133 --> 00:03:47.634
after owners...
[ Audience boos ]

00:03:47.634 --> 00:03:49.033
...failed to reach a deal

00:03:49.033 --> 00:03:51.100
with players to end the lockout,
yeah.

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:52.467
It's tough because that means

00:03:52.467 --> 00:03:54.868
that there's only 900 baseball
games left this season.

00:03:54.868 --> 00:03:57.367
[ Laughter ]

00:03:57.367 --> 00:04:00.133
Yeah, this was rough news
for fans and even more

00:04:00.133 --> 00:04:03.067
devastating news for the tiny
ice cream helmet industry.

00:04:03.067 --> 00:04:05.067
[ Laughter ]

00:04:05.067 --> 00:04:06.334
You guys like that one?

00:04:06.334 --> 00:04:12.634
[ Laughter ]

00:04:12.634 --> 00:04:16.033
Listen to this -- Fitbit is
recalling nearly 2 million

00:04:16.033 --> 00:04:19.567
of its smart watches after
118 people reported

00:04:19.567 --> 00:04:21.601
that the batteries got too hot
and burned them.

00:04:21.601 --> 00:04:22.634
-Ooh.

00:04:22.634 --> 00:04:24.868
-118 people.

00:04:24.868 --> 00:04:26.334
How'd it get to that point?

00:04:26.334 --> 00:04:29.567
Were they like, "Maybe the first
117 are just a fluke"?

00:04:29.567 --> 00:04:31.334
[ Laughter ]

00:04:31.334 --> 00:04:33.267
Usually the only time
I get burned by my Fitbit

00:04:33.267 --> 00:04:35.000
is when it tells me
I didn't stand up enough.

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:37.000
[ Laughter ]

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:38.567
And finally,
this is going viral.

00:04:38.567 --> 00:04:40.267
Last night on
"Wheel of Fortune,"

00:04:40.267 --> 00:04:42.868
one contestant kept trying
to solve the puzzle

00:04:42.868 --> 00:04:45.167
with only two letters left.

00:04:45.167 --> 00:04:48.467
Seemed pretty obvious, but she
just couldn't quite get it.

00:04:48.467 --> 00:04:49.834
Watch this.

00:04:49.834 --> 00:04:51.501
-I'll solve.
-Okay.

00:04:51.501 --> 00:04:54.801
-"Another feather in your hat."

00:04:54.801 --> 00:04:55.734
[ Buzzer ]

00:04:55.734 --> 00:04:57.200
I'll solve.
-Okay.

00:04:57.200 --> 00:05:01.334
-"Another feather in your lap."

00:05:01.334 --> 00:05:02.367
[ Laughter ]
[ Buzzer ]

00:05:02.367 --> 00:05:03.400
-No.

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:04.701
-A P?

00:05:04.701 --> 00:05:07.701
-Yes, there's a P.

00:05:07.701 --> 00:05:09.467
-I will solve.

00:05:09.467 --> 00:05:10.767
-Okay.

00:05:10.767 --> 00:05:15.300
-"Another feather in your map"?

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:16.467
[ Laughter ]

00:05:16.467 --> 00:05:17.968
[ Buzzer ]

00:05:17.968 --> 00:05:23.000
[ Laughter ]

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:25.000
-It was pretty fun though,
'cause during each guess,

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:26.801
we all felt like Chuck Schumer.

